   {
    "name": "Public identity cleanup and proof library lock",
    "insight": "The Stop Line cannot hold if public records conflict or claims are not tied to approved proof.",
    "idea": "Clean buyer-facing public identity, lock approved proof labels and prepare the Key-Message Table before The Stop Line is promoted.",
    "engagement_mechanic": "Internal reviewers and spokespeople use one approved source before any external audience sees the platform.",
    "desired_outcome": "The B Team has a consistent public base for The Stop Line and no public AI claim moves without proof, owner and limit.",
    "targets": "Read public-profile conflict status and proof-label completion at the end of Month 1, then re-read before Month 4 launch.",
